GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "356AAD2A6B2C5BB5"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{3119C8DE63CD7F47}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Overview & Situation"
     m_sContent "Time: 1200 hours; June 27th, 2020"\
     "Location: Takistan"\
     "Weather: Clear skies, Midday"\
     ""\
     "Operation Iron Reclaim"\
     ""\
     "Two days ago, allied Takistani Army forces suffered a critical defeat when Insurgent forces launched a coordinated assault on Rasman Airfield. Outnumbered and overwhelmed, the Takistani garrison was forced to withdraw, leaving behind critical infrastructure, supplies, and air assets."\
     "Intelligence confirms that the Insurgents have fortified the airfield and are using it as a staging ground for further operations in the region."\
     ""\
     "Mission:"\
     "Elements of the United States Army have been mobilized to recapture Rasman Airfield. "\
     ""\
     "End Conditions:"\
     "- 95% Casualty Limit: Defeat"\
     ""\
     "No TL."\
     ""\
     "Mission by Hot Mic"\
     "Feedback is appreciated"\
     ""\
     "Fun Fact:"\
     "This is Hot Mic's second mission for the community."\
     "New Fact: This mission was stuck on review limbo for 4 months because of broken supply helicoptor."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{78FA5F1D76CED79A}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "--- PLAYER ALLOCATION --- [MUST READ]"
     m_sContent "It's important for GM to make sure that the slots are rightly reserved to make this mission fun and somewhat balance. It's also important for CO to understand and set up the proper Chain of Command."\
     ""\
     "     ----- Easy (15 - 27 Players) -----"\
     "1 CHQ, FTO, & Medic"\
     "11 - 22 Troops"\
     "1 Pilot for every 11 Troops"\
     ""\
     "Helicopter Restriction: Transport Helicopter only"\
     ""\
     "     ----- Medium (28 - 53 Players) -----"\
     "1 CHQ & FTO"\
     "2 Medics"\
     ""\
     "22 - 44 Troops"\
     ""\
     "1 Pilot every 11 Troops"\
     "1 Crew every Pilot"\
     ""\
     "Helicopter Restriction: 1 Heavy CAS or 2 Little Birds with Guns & Rockets"\
     ""\
     "   ----- Hard (59 - 85 Players) -----"\
     "1 CHQ & FTO"\
     "2 PHQ"\
     "3 Medics"\
     ""\
     "44 - 66 Troops"\
     ""\
     "3 Pilots"\
     "3 Pilot Crews"\
     ""\
     "Helicopter Restriction: 2 Heavy CAS OR 4 Little Birds with Guns & Rockets OR 1 Heavy CAS and 2 Little Birds with Guns & Rockets"
    }
    GC_Briefing "{97F2E5C4380685C4}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Mission & Mission Notes"
     m_sContent "Phase 1: Sezie Rasman Airfield [Easy]"\
     "Clear hostiles at:"\
     "- North Warehouse Complex"\
     "- Main Warehouse Complex"\
     "- Hangers"\
     "- Oil Depots"\
     ""\
     "Phase 2: Dig in and Defend [Medium & Hard]"\
     "By using Construction truck with the Supplies from MOB. Set up the fortications and defend ATC Tower for 20 minutes."\
     "If the enemy capture it, it's game over for us. "\
     ""\
     "End Conditions:"\
     "- Completing all Objectives: Victory"\
     "-- Defend ATC for 20 minutes."\
     "- 95% Casualty: Defeat"\
     ""\
     "----- Difficuty -----"\
     "Only GM or COs can interact the sign by the ATC to set the difficulty of the mission. It's irreversible action after selecting the option."\
     ""\
     "----- Mission Notes -----"\
     "It's recommanded that recon is needed for the hot insertion"\
     ""\
     "----- Load Plan -----"\
     "Each squad spawns right next to the helicopter. It's recommanded to quicly load up and wait for the Pilot to arrive."\
     ""\
     "--Tickets--"\
     "Easy: 0 Tickets"\
     "Median: 5 Ticktets"\
     "Hard: 10 Tickets"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B39C569DFCF86CFC}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Friendly and Enemy Forces"
     m_sContent "		--- Friendly Forces ---"\
     "1 US Infantry Company"\
     "6x Armed Transport Blackhawks (13 Seats)"\
     ""\
     "Unlimited Blackhawk:"\
     "- Transport (Door Gunners is allowed as CAS)"\
     ""\
     "Unlimited MH-6 Lttle Bird:"\
     "- Transport"\
     "- Supply"\
     "- Guns and/or Unguided Rockets"\
     ""\
     "Unlimited Bell AH-1 Cobra:"\
     "- Guns and Unguided Rockets"\
     ""\
     "Unlimited Boeing AH-64 Apache:"\
     "- Guns and Unguided Rockets"\
     ""\
     "		---Enemy Forces---"\
     "General Situation:"\
     "Local government sympathizers report that the majority of the attacking Insurgent forces have withdrawn from the Military Base. A residual garrison remains stationed within the base perimeter. There are no confirmed enemy patrols operating outside the AO \"Brick\" at this time."\
     ""\
     "Fortified Positions [MEDIUM / HARD]:"\
     "Intelligence confirms that each known Fortified Position (Fort A, B, C, D) is manned by at least one full enemy squad."\
     "Terrain Elevation Advantage (Descending):"\
     "- Fort B (dominant high ground)"\
     "- Fort A"\
     "- Fort C and Fort D (equal and lowest)"\
     ""\
     "Each Fort features 360-degree sandbag fortifications."\
     "WARNING: Each Fort is equipped with a static Anti-Air (AA) emplacement. Additional AA positions are confirmed within AO Brick."\
     ""\
     "Multiple BTRs are present and operational within the base."\
     "Entrenched infantry and hardened defensive positions are expected around key infrastructure."\
     ""\
     "Phase 2 – Enemy Counterattack (Upon Base Capture):"\
     "Upon confirmation of U.S. forces securing Rasman Airfield, the Insurgents are expected to launch an immediate and coordinated counter-offensive from all directions."\
     "Composition:"\
     "Infantry platoons"\
     "Armored support (BTRs)"\
     "Additional AA assets"\
     ""\
     "Prepare for a multi-vector assault targeting the airfield perimeter. Units should be ready to transition to defensive posture and repel enemy reinforcements."\
     ""\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{5F9CC5DE3CF16286}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Command & Signal"
     m_sContent "LR Channels:"\
     "Company Net: 48.0 Mhz (Default)"\
     "Platoon 1 Net: 48.5 Mhz"\
     "Platoon 2 Net: 47.5 MHz"\
     ""\
     "Air Net: 49 MHz"\
     ""\
     "Personnel:"\
     "Company HQ: Overlord"\
     "- Platoon 1 HQ: 1'6"\
     "-- 1st Squad: 1'1"\
     "-- 2nd Squad: 1'2"\
     "-- 3rd Squad: 1'3"\
     "- Patoon 2 HQ: 2'6"\
     "-- 1st Squad: 2'1"\
     "-- 2nd Squad: 2'2"\
     "-- 3rd Squad: 2'3"\
     ""\
     "Second in Charge: Always refer as {CO Callsign} Minor"\
     ""\
     "Airgroup:"\
     "Supply/Transport: Mule {1, 2, ect.}"\
     "CAS: Donkey {1, 2, ect.}"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CDC0F1542EFCAE25}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Supplies and Support"
     m_sContent "a. Aviation / Close Air Support:"\
     "- The Main Operating Base (MoB) maintains unlimited Refuel amd Rearm for CAS support."\
     "- Forward Air Controllers (FAC) must coordinate strikes in accordance with ROE (Type 3)."\
     ""\
     "b. Infantry Resupply:"\
     "Infantry elements are equipped with the following at MoB:"\
     "- Arsenal Crate"\
     "- Supply Crate"\
     "- Medical Box"\
     ""\
     "c. Sandbags:"\
     "Each starting helicopter carries 78 sandbags plus huge backpack."\
     "Suppy Crate carries unlimited amount of sandbags. "\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{431F7F93AA22538F}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Notes for GM and Pilots"
     m_sContent "GM: If there isn't enough AI or AI isn't apply enough pressure to the defenders during Phase 2; spawn new AI groups if possible. Feel free to take manual controls of AA units. If there are too much AI, you can delete some units or in worst case, head to the CO's Pit and use the Debug Sign to clear the AI Respawns Flags."\
     ""\
     "Pilots: They are free to take what ever helicopters they want. Ideally, they must work in pairs, in the same helicopter. "\
     ""\
     "Heavy CAS definition: Any Helicopter that need two people to function."\
     ""
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
